 "mosaic_detail": 1.2,
 "mosaic_interp": "LINEAR",
 "_mosaic": "a ground is a soft field of close colours in metres (LINEAR between them, in this order), never hard blobs of far ones: hard blobs of red, grey and black read as camouflage (his NO on the casino carpet, 10/22)",
 "_sand_in_the_palette": "the sand family (the measure's own test: L 30-86, C 5-40, h 45-105) holds the dead lawn, the dun stucco, the plywood, the rust and the desert's grey-brown; each is one choice among greys, darks and stained concrete, never a whole theme, so the map stays under a third at every zoom",
 "mosaic_soften": 0.32,
 "_mosaic_soften": "each ground's colours are pulled this far toward the ground's own mean before the ramp: the yard still varies, it never reads as camouflage",
 "_era": "rule 159(d) and 128 (Paolo 10/24: 'maybe in act three things get better, part of that transformation over time'): the 10/24 bright dials (lawns gone wild, pools, painted stucco, tile) are ACT THREE's, the world healed; render them with BOHEMIA_COLOUR_DIALS=banks/BOHEMIA_MAP_COLOUR_DIALS_ACT3_THE_HEALED_10_24_26.json when act three starts (rule 128(d): not before he is happy with act one)",
 "keep_sat": 0.55,
 "_keep_sat": "a face of the factory's scene that was not sand (the barn's red, a sign, the glass) keeps its colour at this saturation: act one x0.55, act three x1.25 (10/24's, which pushed them brighter)",
 "_accents": "159(c): the Strip's neon (neon_*) is kept at full strength and appears only on the glitz fences and signs (the painting refuses neon on a roof or a wall); the faded tarp (one roof in ten in the houses), the faded red door (one wall in nine in the blocks and the farms' barns); a faction's colour on its ground is the territory code's"
}